    "summary": "Plan-only ACCEPT at transition-0062. The corrected architecture gives the batch a direct Identity and database authority path while Web selects its complete management and October dataset through startup configuration; the default co-locates Identity, with an explicit separate Identity option. It preserves exact batch isolation, historical context provenance, provider binding, ordinary startup and Story 18.1's approval, issuer, current-authority verifier, context lifetime and three closed Worker functions. Prior P-18.4-01 through P-18.4-05 and D-18.4-01 through D-18.4-05 were compared with the current plan and present no open plan defect; the superseded Web transport is explicitly removed. Workflow validation, explicit implementation-design validation and scoped diff check passed. Full SpecKit task analysis is deferred because the existing tasks belong to the superseded plan. The corrected plan changes architecture through headless Identity reuse, direct current database authority and a generator-to-Web assembly reference. It needs fresh scoped planned-change authorization before task reconciliation. No AGENTS.md Worker-tool, Scan-strategy or PRD-change trigger is established. Existing approvals do not approve this revised architecture, implementation or runtime resources. The ongoing recovery episode remains at 6 of 7."
